{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1205049-cast-forward-in-time","id":1205049,"title":"Cast Forward in Time","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-09T19:17:00-07:00","id":1205049,"title":"Cast Forward in Time","content":"Well met, friends. I have a backstory idea I want to run past the forum to gauge it on a scale of &quot;Novel, and interesting&quot; to &quot;You are a rule breaking Mary Sue&quot;. I jest, but here's the pitch-<br /> <br /> In the First Age, sometime after the Primordial Wars, a great Behemoth known as World Eater Levantan rampaged in the South. It wholly destroyed the Jewelled City Dunesong, as that fabled town and it's Tower of Ivory were built on top of a leyline nexus, and Levantan was made to clear obstructions in the Geomantic Leyline system and reshape geography for it's Primordial masters. Now that it has &quot;slipped the leash&quot;, the sentient shovel creature had to be stopped. A great battle was waged and Ibram, the prince of Dunesong dove into the creatures great mouth to destroy the source of it's terrible thunderous screech, which had toppled walls and laid waste to many heroic soldiers. Struck down by the Solar Exalted, the great beast went into a terrible death throw, and it's world-shaping power tore a hole in the fabric of time itself, casting it and the mortal prince forward by centuries. It's final rest has come, and the prince emerges into the Time of Sorrows, taking with him three things- the Second Breath, the contemporary knowledge of the First Age, and the Artifact Thunder's Cry, made from the blue-jade infused vocal cords of Levantan.<br /> <br /> tl;dr a guy from the first age is cast forward to the present. Is time-travel forward forbidden?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T19:42:43-07:00","id":1205063,"title":"","content":"There have been a number of figures in the setting who overtly or implicitly spent extended periods of time in some kind of stasis, to emerge in the Time of Tumult. Dragon Kings have done it, Magnificent Jaguar did it, and there were some comics that wanted to imply that the nameless Solar who wielded Righteous Devil Style did it. Also one guy who was heir to the Shogunate, and crystallized right before he would have Exalted.<br /> <br /> \u200bI find the difference between being locked in a crystal stasis chamber or going into a magical hibernation, and being caught up in some kind of strange cosmic effect that causes you to skip forward a large portion of time, to be largely academic. After all, everything is <i>already</i> travelling forward in time, it's just about different methods of ensuring that you'll be around to meet it.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe significance of time travel being a no go is in not letting players mess around with the consequences of their actions; that you don't get do-overs or to return to a preferable state of affairs, nor do you get to heavily interact with the way that things might be before returning to the &quot;present&quot; and using that knowledge to adjust your own actions.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo I say, sure, go with it. It's not as if the setting contains a time portal that they can use to return home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T21:06:51-07:00","id":1205082,"title":"","content":"I had my own version of the tl;dr aummery. I used Wyld exploration though.<br /> <br /> I think the point of the no time travel rule is to prevent changing the past. It's about no backsies on consequences (see alsog resurrection). Bu someone going forward with no way back can work","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T21:12:15-07:00","id":1205084,"title":"","content":"I'm all for it, I've introduced characters timelost before, and in my last game a bunch of orphans funneled into a city from the catacombs below that turned out to be clones from the first age whose stasis chambers were disrupted. I'm all for quirky time journeymen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T03:26:24-07:00","id":1205129,"title":"","content":"has anyone done a timelost DB? or is it always Celestials?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T03:54:56-07:00","id":1205130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1205049-cast-forward-in-time?p=1205129#post1205129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">has anyone done a timelost DB? or is it always Celestials?</div> </div> </div> </div>In one of my many settings variations there is a lost continent deep in the west that was flung forward in time, and it is heavily populated with Dragon Blooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T06:17:36-07:00","id":1205161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1205049-cast-forward-in-time?p=1205129#post1205129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">has anyone done a timelost DB? or is it always Celestials?</div> </div> </div> </div>Had one who was preserved in a white jade sarcophagus. She was gonna wake up and be terrifying","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T14:56:22-07:00","id":1205374,"title":"","content":"I was thinking of a First Age DB cast forward and the shock of one finding a world where his kind are in charge and Celestials ate considered monsters.<br /> <br /> And the confusion of modern DBs to his not getting why","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T15:37:57-07:00","id":1205392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1205049-cast-forward-in-time?p=1205374#post1205374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking of a First Age DB cast forward and the shock of one finding a world where his kind are in charge and Celestials ate considered monsters.<br /> <br /> And the confusion of modern DBs to his not getting why</div> </div> </div> </div>In my setting, a Twilight Solar who refused the Calibration feast was tracked to her Island sanctuary, where she proceeded to try and set off an experimental device that should have stopped time, but it malfunctioned, and slowed it instead. 100 years passed for every minute since it's activation, until at last she was killed, and the bloody, decimated, but victorious legions managed to destroy the device. Now they find themselves exiles, lost in the sea of time. In 2e the island was in the South West, but since 3e added The Caul about where they were, I'll probably put them in the far North West instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T23:10:57-07:00","id":1205472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1205049-cast-forward-in-time?p=1205129#post1205129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">has anyone done a timelost DB? or is it always Celestials?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've heard it a few times during 2e, almost always done to justify having Legendary Breeding and being able to know where all the setting's shiniest stuff is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T06:37:22-07:00","id":1205568,"title":"","content":"In my game my players just fought off a Solar whi piggy-backed on the back end if an Exaltation through a combination of Sidereal Astrology and Divine hijinks. After a helluva battle inside the mind/souls scape of the Solar PC under the invasion the PC's have ended up with a &quot;memory box&quot; containing the identity and knowledge of the dispaced would-be god king.<br /> <br /> Now the PC whose mind was initially invaded gets to decide if the knowledge of that dead Solar is worth giving up a portion of his identity (intimacies and principles).<br /> <br /> Not exactly what you're talking about, but it's become an interesting dilemma for my group that they're still mulling over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T07:11:20-07:00","id":1205578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1205049-cast-forward-in-time?p=1205130#post1205130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In one of my many settings variations there is a lost continent deep in the west that was flung forward in time, and it is heavily populated with Dragon Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a cool adventure for the later game. An entire armada of high Essence Dragon Bloods pop into Creation, find out what's going on and learn about the lack of the Scarlet Empress and decide to expand their power base throughout the West... That's a rad hook. They'd also have no loyalty to the status quo of The Realm. Stolen for later!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T15:08:51-07:00","id":1205772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1205049-cast-forward-in-time?p=1205578#post1205578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a cool adventure for the later game. An entire armada of high Essence Dragon Bloods pop into Creation, find out what's going on and learn about the lack of the Scarlet Empress and decide to expand their power base throughout the West... That's a rad hook. They'd also have no loyalty to the status quo of The Realm. Stolen for later!</div> </div> </div> </div>They were a bit more desperate then that, having just lost 20% of their #, and most of them were of high essence, to a mad solar god queen &quot;just the other day&quot;, but yes, it was a good &quot;WTF&quot; moment for my players when they realized what was going on. If anyone is interested in knowing more about it let me know and I'll see if I can dig up the doc I wrote up about it and post it to google docs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T16:03:22-07:00","id":1205800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1205049-cast-forward-in-time?p=1205772#post1205772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They were a bit more desperate then that, having just lost 20% of their #, and most of them were of high essence, to a mad solar god queen &amp;quot;just the other day&amp;quot;, but yes, it was a good &amp;quot;WTF&amp;quot; moment for my players when they realized what was going on. If anyone is interested in knowing more about it let me know and I'll see if I can dig up the doc I wrote up about it and post it to google docs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please share!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T16:11:32-07:00","id":1205803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1205049-cast-forward-in-time?p=1205800#post1205800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please share!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll try and post it later tonight after my twins go down.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T16:20:04-07:00","id":1205811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1205049-cast-forward-in-time?p=1205578#post1205578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a cool adventure for the later game. An entire armada of high Essence Dragon Bloods pop into Creation, find out what's going on and learn about the lack of the Scarlet Empress and decide to expand their power base throughout the West... That's a rad hook. They'd also have no loyalty to the status quo of The Realm. Stolen for later!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought of this trying to imagine Gens Iza returning from its expedition. or at least a fleet led by Dragon Bloods. They'd probably bit low on supplies though depending how long the voyage took from their perspective.<br /> <br /> And may have had some adult Golden Children along since the flag ship needed solar essence attunement to run","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T13:43:18-07:00","id":1208154,"title":"","content":"Btw, did I ever mention my idea about the effect on Denandsor being caused by time phase shifting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T14:20:49-07:00","id":1208175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1205049-cast-forward-in-time?p=1205129#post1205129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">has anyone done a timelost DB? or is it always Celestials?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've done it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1205049-cast-forward-in-time?p=1205472#post1205472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've heard it a few times during 2e, almost always done to justify having Legendary Breeding and being able to know where all the setting's shiniest stuff is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also in the case of my Wood Aspect Iza Iyanna, I portrayed her as a put-upon university student with a collection of Celestial Exalt memorabilia (the fact she met some who wanted to be her friend was amazing!) compared to a career soldier or an aristocrat.<br /> <br /> If you think Doc from Red vs. Blue you'd be in the right ballpark for her demeanour though actually competent.<br /> <br /> In some ways it was a deliberate deconstruction of what a lot of people on the forum seemed to be expecting from a First Age Dragon-Blooded with Legendary Breeding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 04-17-2018, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T05:55:00-07:00","id":1208407,"title":"","content":"I've had a few time-lost NPCs (through magical stasis rather than timey-wimey shenanigans, but as others have pointed out, the difference is mostly academic for one-way trips forward).<br /> <br /> My favourite is Marisol, the Golden Child daughter of a Solar queen and her raksha husband (political marriage). Marisol's mother killed her father during one of his bedlam-induced outbursts, despite genuinely caring for him, because the marriage was no longer politically convenient and restraining him was a hassle (the Great Curse is a bitch). This was traumatising enough for the kid, but rather than deal with her daughter's grief, the Solar decided to use sorcery to encase her child in crystal until such a time as she could be bothered to be a parent to her again. Then the Usurpation happened.<br /> <br /> Fast forward to when the PCs are exploring this hidden manse and find the sleeping princess. They free her. You have to understand, this girl's mother tucked her in one night, promising they'd talk in the morning, and she woke up more than a thousand years later to find her home abandoned, everyone she ever knew and loved long dead, and a group of strangers staring at her. Needless to say, it took them a while to calm her down, and longer to help her deal with what had happened. They ended up giving her into the care of a clucky elder Lunar who had lost her Solar adopted daughter in the Usurpation (and had spent half the time since in grief-induced hibernation), and the two kind of completed each other. <br /> <br /> Time-lost characters are great for fish-out-of-water stories (even after they adjust, playing someone with an outsider's perspective is fun), and for introducing anachronisms that you'd like to play with (I had a dragonblooded pirate NPC who was an archery specialist in an age of firearms and kevlar because he followed his Lunar love into magical slumber).<br /> <br /> For PCs, they're definitely the sort of concept you'd want to run past your Storyteller to make sure they're not going to disrupt the themes and tone of the game, not to mention the plot. Using the trope to justify convenient knowledge of the setting is a bit on the nose, and your ST should absolutely play up the set-backs you encounter as a result of being out of the loop for centuries. But as long as the time-travel is a one-off forward-jump, the concept isn't setting breaking. As for whether it's a Mary Sue, that depends on how you play the character more than anything, I'd say. If you dominate every scene with your wacky lack of understanding or historical trivia, then yes. If you roleplay a person struggling to find their bearings in a new and unfamiliar world in a poignant and nuanced way that doesn't hog the spotlight, then no. It'll also depend on your group. Some people might find the character grating, others might play off them really well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T04:45:12-07:00","id":1213376,"title":"","content":"I have a homebrew Exalt type who approach this idea but in a different way to a lot of the examples in the thread.<br /> In their case their Exaltation takes an indefinite amount of time to catalyse during which time they enter suspended animation and are sealed in sarcophagi. For most of them their awakening is years or decades later and more coming to terms with life moving on without them but they can be flexible, like someone who knew the Perfect of Paragon when he was a scavenger lord or wakes up in Chiaroscuro wondering what the Delzhan are doing there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T11:12:57-07:00","id":1419193,"title":"","content":"(might count as thread necromancy) <br /> <br /> i think time travel is impossible in exalted. but then again, it was impossible for the primordials to die. the exalted are made to do the impossible","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}